@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Cookie Policy";
}

<h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
<p class="text-muted">Last updated: @DateTime.Now.ToString("dd MMMM yyyy")</p>
<hr />

<p>This Cookie Policy explains how TracKeee, operated by Carolina Maria Vorster, uses cookies and similar technologies when you visit and use our service.</p>

<h4 class="mt-4">1. What Are Cookies</h4>
<p>Cookies are small text files stored on your device (computer, tablet, or phone) when you visit a website. They help the website remember your actions and preferences over time.</p>

<h4 class="mt-4">2. Cookies We Use</h4>

<h5 class="mt-3">Essential Cookies (Required)</h5>
<p>These cookies are necessary for TracKeee to function. They cannot be disabled.</p>

<div class="table-responsive">
    <table class="table table-sm">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Cookie</th>
                <th>Purpose</th>
                <th>Duration</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><code>.AspNetCore.Identity.Application</code></td>
                <td>Keeps you logged in to your account</td>
                <td>Session / 14 days if "Remember me" is selected</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>.AspNetCore.Antiforgery</code></td>
                <td>Protects against cross-site request forgery (security)</td>
                <td>Session</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>.AspNetCore.CookieConsent</code></td>
                <td>Remembers your cookie consent preference</td>
                <td>365 days</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

<h5 class="mt-3">Analytics Cookies (Not Currently Used)</h5>
<p>TracKeee does not currently use any analytics or tracking cookies. We do not use Google Analytics, Facebook Pixel, or any other third-party tracking tools.</p>

<h5 class="mt-3">Advertising Cookies</h5>
<p>TracKeee does not use any advertising or marketing cookies.</p>

<h4 class="mt-4">3. Third-Party Cookies</h4>
<p>When you use the Yoco payment feature, Yoco's payment page may set its own cookies. These cookies are governed by <a href="https://www.yoco.com/za/legal/privacy-policy/" target="_blank">Yoco's Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

<h4 class="mt-4">4. Managing Cookies</h4>
<p>You can control cookies through your browser settings. Most browsers allow you to:</p>
<ul>
    <li>View what cookies are stored</li>
    <li>Delete individual or all cookies</li>
    <li>Block cookies from specific or all websites</li>
    <li>Set preferences for certain types of cookies</li>
</ul>
<p>Please note that disabling essential cookies will prevent you from logging in and using TracKeee.</p>

<h4 class="mt-4">5. Your Rights Under POPIA</h4>
<p>Under the Protection of Personal Information Act (POPIA), you have the right to know what personal information is being collected and how it is used. Essential cookies are permitted under POPIA as they are necessary for the functioning of the service. For more details on your rights, see our <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

<h4 class="mt-4">6. Changes to This Policy</h4>
<p>We may update this Cookie Policy if we introduce new cookies or change how we use existing ones. Changes will be posted on this page with an updated date.</p>

